  "version": "v1.0",
  "release_date": "2025-11-19T00:00:00Z",
  "updated": "2025-11-19T00:00:00Z",
  "description": "TESSERA is a pixel-wise, multi-modal (Sentinel-1/2) remote sensing foundation model that learns robust, label-efficient embeddings from irregular, sparse EO time series. It uses Barlow Twins self-supervised learning, global shuffling, and mix-based regularization to produce global, annual, 10m, int8 embeddings for every land pixel, enabling state-of-the-art performance on classification, segmentation, and regression tasks with minimal computation and high label efficiency.",
  "sci:doi": "10.48550/arXiv.2506.20380",
